{"id":"chatcmpl-63365d93-68aa-4f03-b5c4-f825de81e057","object":"chat.completion","created":1795246465,"model":"deepseek-v4.1-flash","choices":[{"index":0,"message":{"role":"assistant","reasoning_content":"","content":"```json\n{\n  \"highlights\": \"This task resolves a binary laterality question (left vs right) about a radiographic finding by combining expert visual description, grounded localization, and phrase grounding against orientation markers. The key insight is that laterality must be verified against explicit image orientation metadata rather than assumed from visual appearance, since radiological images are conventionally displayed mirrored. Multiple independent localization methods were cross-checked before committing to an answer.\",\n  \"patterns\": [\n    \"When a question hinges on spatial laterality (left/right, upper/lower), explicitly query orientation markers or metadata before interpreting visual position, because display convention may invert apparent sides.\",\n    \"Decompose a binary diagnostic question into (a) expert descriptive analysis, (b) grounded localization with coordinates, and (c) targeted phrase grounding for each candidate finding, then reconcile the three.\",\n    \"Use phrase grounding on the specific candidate answer text to confirm presence and location, rather than relying solely on a free-form report.\",\n    \"Cross-validate findings across independent tools (expert description, grounded report, phrase grounding) and only answer when they converge on the same side/location.\"\n  ],\n  \"playbooks\": {\n    \"Medical imaging interpretation\": \"Always resolve patient-side laterality using orientation markers/metadata before mapping visual position to anatomical side; treat image-left as patient-right by default in radiology.\",\n    \"Binary diagnostic multiple-choice\": \"Ground each candidate option separately against the image and select the one with confirmed localization rather than eliminating by absence alone.\",\n    \"Multi-tool evidence fusion\": \"Combine a descriptive expert pass, a coordinate-grounded localization pass, and a targeted phrase-grounding pass; require agreement before finalizing.\"\n  },\n  \"checklists\": [\n    \"Confirm image orientation (markers/metadata) and map visual left/right to patient left/right before answering.\",\n    \"Verify the chosen finding is positively localized by at least two independent methods (grounded report + phrase grounding).\"\n  ]\n}\n```"},"finish_reason":"stop","logprobs":null}],"usage":{"prompt_tokens":513,"total_tokens":920,"completion_tokens":407,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":0,"image_tokens":0,"text_tokens":513},"completion_tokens_details":{"text_tokens":407}}}